From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Task 11: in-CRM agent softphone panel (fork UI)

Adds the browser half of the transferred-call softphone: a Twilio Voice JS
Device owned by the sidebar (mounted on every dashboard page, same reasoning
as 0057's inbound alerts), a floating ring/in-call panel teleported to
<body>, and the three small backend calls it needs
(POST /voice/agent/{token,heartbeat,unregister} -- Task 4's endpoints).
Nothing on the backend is touched by this patch.

THREE NEW FILES, ONE TWO-HUNK EDIT.

  api/protonVoice.js            -- the three backend calls
  composables/useProtonSoftphone.js -- owns the Twilio Device for this tab
  components-next/softphone/ProtonSoftphonePanel.vue -- the ring/in-call UI
  components-next/sidebar/Sidebar.vue -- imports + mounts the panel

AUTH FORWARDING IS COPIED, NOT REINVENTED. protonVoice.js's voiceRequest()
forwards the devise_token_auth access-token/client/uid triplet from
Auth.getAuthData() exactly the way protonAdmin.js's adminRequest() does (see
patch 0030) -- plus x-api-key from useProtonConfig()'s backendKey. This is
deliberately per-USER, not the shared-secret path: /voice/agent/* is gated by
require_permission_with_identity (Task 4), because the whole point of the
token endpoint is minting a Twilio access token IN THE CALLING AGENT'S OWN
NAME. There is nothing for a request body to say about identity here -- the
backend derives it from the session these headers prove, and ignores
anything else.

GATED TWICE, BOTH REQUIRED. The mount in Sidebar.vue only renders when
`protonHasFeature('agent_softphone')` (the tenant's PROTON_FEATURES list,
0001/0002's mechanism) AND `protonHasPermission('voice.answer')` (RBAC,
0025's mechanism) are both true. `protonHasFeature` and `protonHasPermission`
are already destructured in Sidebar.vue by patches 0002 and 0025 respectively
-- this patch does not re-declare them, only adds the one new import and the
one new template line that use them.

WHY MOUNTED FROM THE SIDEBAR AND NOT A DEDICATED ROUTE. Same reasoning as
0057's inbound alerts: the sidebar is on every dashboard page, and a phone
that only rings while the agent happens to have a specific route open is not
a phone. ProtonSoftphonePanel teleports itself to <body> (Vue 3's built-in
<Teleport>, not a Chatwoot component), so it floats above the whole app
rather than being clipped by the sidebar's own layout -- this is exactly why
this patch adds no markup to Sidebar's own visual tree, only a single
conditional child element right before </aside>, the same shape 0057 used
for its status strip except this one DOES need a template slot (the ring UI
has to be interactive, the alert strip did not).

THE THREE-CALL SHAPE (token / heartbeat / unregister) matches Task 4's
router 1:1: register() fetches a token and calls Device.register(), then
heartbeats every 30s so the backend's fan-out knows this tab is live, and
unregister() fires from onBeforeUnmount so a closed tab drops out of the
fan-out quickly rather than waiting out a heartbeat timeout (Task 12
scenario F). tokenWillExpire re-fetches and calls device.updateToken() so a
long session does not silently drop off Twilio's registry mid-shift.

THE NEUTRAL "CALL ENDED" STATE (endWith('ended')) exists because Twilio's
Voice SDK fires the SAME `cancel` event whether a colleague answered first or
the caller simply hung up while this tab was still ringing, and this fork has
no server-push channel to ask the backend which one happened (Task 12
scenario L is exactly this race). Guessing "answered by another agent" would
be a confident lie roughly half the time, so the panel shows a neutral
"Call ended" for 3 seconds and then quietly resets -- long enough that the
agent does not mistake it for a misclick, short enough that it does not sit
there looking broken. `reject()` (this agent explicitly declining) skips that
state and closes immediately, since they already know what happened.

FAIL-QUIET BY DESIGN. Every catch block in useProtonSoftphone.js sets
`status = 'error'` or silently swallows (heartbeat failures, unregister on
unmount, tokenWillExpire refresh) rather than throwing into the CRM. A
softphone that breaks the dashboard around it would be worse for an agent
than one that simply does not ring; the failure mode this patch accepts is
"this tab silently drops out of the fan-out," which Task 12's manual
verification plan (scenario F) exists to catch by observation, since nothing
in the browser would otherwise say so out loud.

NO `Button` COMPONENT, AND WHY. Chatwoot's own `Button` props and `n-*`
colour tokens are not verifiable from this sandboxed checkout -- there is no
built dashboard to inspect. Per the task brief's own instruction,
ProtonSlaPoliciesPage.vue (patch 0025) was read as the cross-check, and it
turns out to answer the question outright: that page does not use `Button`
ANYWHERE. Every action in it is a plain `<button>` styled with Tailwind and
the `n-*` tokens this fork's other already-merged patches actually use in
real, applied hunks -- `bg-n-brand` + `text-white` for a primary action
(0010, 0012, 0025 all use exactly this), `text-n-ruby-9` for a destructive
one (0010, 0012), `border-n-weak` / `bg-n-alpha-black1` / `bg-n-background` /
`text-n-slate-11` / `text-n-slate-12` for the rest (0005, 0010, 0011, 0012,
0013, 0025 all use these). ProtonSoftphonePanel.vue follows that same
established pattern instead of guessing a component API that a wrong prop
would render broken, not fail to build. The one token that is inference
rather than direct confirmation is the `/10` opacity modifier applied to
`text-n-ruby-9` for the Reject/Hang-up hover state (`hover:bg-n-ruby-9/10`)
-- the modifier itself is confirmed elsewhere (0012 uses `bg-n-brand/10`),
just not this exact colour+modifier pairing.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` was run against the real
chatwoot/chatwoot:v4.15.1 Sidebar.vue (fetched directly, not reconstructed)
for both of this patch's Sidebar.vue hunks, and both are anchored on regions
NONE of patches 0001-0068 touch (the trailing import block and the
</aside>-adjacent markup), so that check is a direct, not a synthetic,
verification -- unlike 0053-0057's synthetic pre-image reconstructions. The
three new files cannot be applied-checked the same way (they have no upstream
counterpart to diff against); their correctness is unverified beyond local
review. Cloud Build (`gcloud builds submit`, Step 6 of the task) was
DELIBERATELY NOT RUN THIS SESSION -- it needs the tenant's Artifact Registry
substitution and credentials this session does not have. The actual
`pnpm exec vite build` compiling this Vue code (and thus catching any Vue
syntax error, import-path typo, or the Button-API question above at the only
point that would actually catch it) remains OWED, exactly like 0057's own
still-owed screenshot verification.

Build via Cloud Build for amd64 once merged; never on the prod VM, never from
an arm64 Mac.
